# Nginx Proxy Manager hosts

## Gate

Use when the user authorized Nginx Proxy Manager (NPM) work and the turn
needs **proxy hosts**, **redirection hosts**, or **streams** inventory/craft.
SSL-only → `nginx-proxy-manager-ssl`. Access-list-only →
`nginx-proxy-manager-access`. Delete/disable → also
`nginx-proxy-manager-safety`.

## Transport (no NPM MCP discovered)

No Nginx Proxy Manager MCP was found for this harness. Prefer, in order:

1. Checked-in export/backup JSON or IaC that names host ids/domains.
2. Product **REST API** against an operator-resolved base URL (scheme + host
   + port) with a short-lived Bearer token from `/api/tokens` — never hardcode
   the instance URL; never paste tokens into chat.
3. Authenticated admin UI when API access is unavailable.

If an MCP appears later, use its list/get tools when ready — **do not invent
MCP tool names**.

## API inventory map (HTTP)

Resolve `BASE` from operator config/env/ask this turn. Auth: `POST {BASE}/api/tokens`
with identity the user authorized; use `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on
subsequent calls; do not echo the token.

| Need | Method + path |
| --- | --- |
| List proxy hosts | `GET /api/nginx/proxy-hosts` |
| One proxy host | `GET /api/nginx/proxy-hosts/{id}` |
| Create proxy host | `POST /api/nginx/proxy-hosts` |
| Update proxy host | `PUT /api/nginx/proxy-hosts/{id}` |
| Delete proxy host | `DELETE /api/nginx/proxy-hosts/{id}` (safety gate) |
| List redirections | `GET /api/nginx/redirection-hosts` |
| One / mutate redirection | `GET|POST|PUT|DELETE /api/nginx/redirection-hosts[/{id}]` |
| List streams | `GET /api/nginx/streams` |
| One / mutate stream | `GET|POST|PUT|DELETE /api/nginx/streams[/{id}]` |
| Dead hosts (404) | `GET /api/nginx/dead-hosts` (+ mutate only with explicit verb) |

Confirm path shapes against the running NPM version when a call 404s —
minor releases can rename fields; prefer list-then-get evidence.

## Discover first

1. Never invent proxy-host, redirection, or stream **ids** — list this turn
   or use exact ids/domains the user pasted.
2. Resolve domain → id via list filter before update/delete.
3. Before retargeting upstream, show current `forward_host` / `forward_port`
   / scheme from get evidence.
4. Cap large lists; summarize and offer domain or enabled filters.

## Craft defaults

1. Prefer **update-in-place** (`PUT` by id) over delete+recreate for domain
   or upstream changes.
2. State domain names, forward scheme (`http`/`https`), forward host + port,
   and whether websockets / HTTP2 / HSTS flags were set — from ask or
   existing object.
3. Do not enable `allow_websocket_upgrade` or cache bypass flags unless asked
   or copying an evidenced host.
4. Certificate and access-list **ids** on a host must come from
   `nginx-proxy-manager-ssl` / `nginx-proxy-manager-access` inventory — never
   invent foreign keys.
5. Apex and mail-adjacent hosts: call out blast radius (www, MX-adjacent
   HTTP, API subdomains) before mutate.

## Report shape

- **id** + **domain_names**
- **forward** — scheme://host:port
- **enabled** / **ssl** summary (cert id or “none”)
- **access_list_id** when set
- **type** — proxy | redirection | stream

## Out of scope

- Certificate issue/renew details → `nginx-proxy-manager-ssl`
- Access list CIDR craft → `nginx-proxy-manager-access`
- Other reverse-proxy products’ APIs
- DNS record edits

